# The component sources are the source of truth: `tb-ah-run-js/`, `tb-ah-render-jinja/`,
# `tb-ah-query-tbdb/`, `runtime/`, `migrations/`, `tools/` and the two textproto files.
# `traildepot/` is a build artefact assembled from them by clear_db.bat + build.bat, so everything
# in it is generated and git-ignored.
traildepot/config.textproto
traildepot/metadata.textproto
traildepot/migrations/
traildepot/runtime/

# TrailBase runtime state.
traildepot/data/
traildepot/backups/
traildepot/uploads/
traildepot/secrets/
traildepot/wasm/
*.log
# A hand-taken copy of `data/` before a schema change. `traildepot/backups/` is TrailBase's own and
# is ignored above, but a copy made by hand lands beside it and is a 95 MB database: never staged.
traildepot/backup-*/
# A hand-taken copy of `data/` before a rebuild/import (e.g. `data.pre-parity-<ts>`): a full database.
traildepot/data.pre-*/
# The bench orchestrator redirects the server's streams to `*.log.err`, which `*.log` misses.
traildepot/*.log.*

# Rust build output for the guest components.
#
# These rules must NOT be indented: git treats leading whitespace in a .gitignore line as part of
# the pattern, so an indented `component/target/` matches no path at all. That silently happened
# here — `host/target/` sat indented for the whole life of this file, so the build output was
# never ignored and only stayed out of commits because nobody ran `git add trailbase/host`.
target/

# Throw-away depot the tools create when they run.
.tbdemo-guest/
.tbdemo-invview/
.tbdemo-ui/

runtime/vaulter-lite/

# The assembled distributable (dist.ps1 / dist.bat output). Rebuildable, never committed.
dist/

# The built Go control panel binary; `controlpanel/` is the source and IS committed.
controlpanel.exe
controlpanel/controlpanel.exe
